All of the simulated samples are processed through a full simulation of the CMS detector based on Geant4 [45] and are normalized to their predicted cross section described in Refs. [46–49]. The effects of pileup are included in the simulation and the pileup distribution in simulation is weighted to match the pileup in the data. The jet energy response and resolution in simulated events are corrected to match the data [24]. In addition, the b-jet identification (b tagging) efficiency and misidentification rate [25], and the lepton trigger and reconstruction efficiencies are corrected in simulation [28, 30].Fig. 1
